{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdjkthv7ePvgZp5vd7v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XjiF7NN8bhaDPUvVKkiXrT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-n3kslw9k/skill && PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; F=../agent/brace-findings.json\na(){ $PY scripts/answer.py $F \"$@\" 2>&1 | tail -3; }\na check B01.1 --met no --evidence app/extractor.py:25 --quote 'EXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"' --note 'tools.yaml:14 defines role \"extractor\", not \"line_item_extractor\". build_registry (tools/__init__.py:69) falls back to the procurement list for an unknown role, so the sub-agent that reads untrusted documents gets all nine procurement tools, including pay_invoice and erp_call, not only read_document.'\na check B01.2 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:110 --quote 'self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}' --note 'refresh_tools (also run on tools/list_changed, mcp_client.py:105) replaces the tool set with no pin check, no metadata scan and no allowlist filter. initialize pins by fingerprint only (mcp_client.py:95-98), which is not a role allowlist. erp_call then reaches any discovered ERP operation that starts with a gate prefix (gate.py:35).'\na check B01.3 --met no --evidence app/tools/erp.py:27 --quote 'return await erp.call(args[\"operation\"], arguments, ident, deps.erp_scope_for(args[\"operation\"]))' --note 'The top-level dispatcher rejects unknown tool names (loop.py:59-65). erp_call is a second dispatcher: it passes a model-chosen ERP operation name straight to the MCP server. Any discovered operation that starts with a gate prefix, e.g. invoice.void or vendor.update_remit_to, is callable, so the real allowlist is a prefix list and not exact names.'\na check B02.2 --met no --evidence app/tools/memory.py:44 --quote 'business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant' 