{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdqkhxgc2VdXbqQmCzF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the B01–B05 batch review. The findings file is saved at `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges` with 4 gaps and 1 needs_evidence. I did not run challenges, as you asked.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B01 | gap | The sub-agent role is `line_item_extractor` in `app/extractor.py:25`, but `config/tools.yaml:14` calls it `extractor`. The registry falls back to the full procurement tool list (`app/tools/__init__.py:69`), so the sub-agent that reads untrusted documents gets `pay_invoice` and `erp_call`. `refresh_tools` (`app/mcp_client.py:107-111`) also skips the pin check and metadata scan. |\n| B02 | gap | `memory_read` takes `business_unit` from a model-filled argument (`app/tools/memory.py:44`). The database uses one shared login with no row-level security. |\n| B03 | needs_evidence | I found no checked-in secrets. The STS token lifetimes, the source of the Anthropic key (`app/main.py:96`) and holder-binding support are not in this repo. |\n| B04 | gap | The only operator stop is a database flag the agent reads once at run start (`app/loop.py:127`). Nothing revokes issued tokens or in-flight runs, and no revocation time limit is stated. |\n| B05 | gap | `app/gate.py:35` is an unanchored prefix test. It lets `invoice.void`, `invoice.mark_paid` and `vendor.update_remit_to` skip approval, and `config/policy.yaml:22-26` grants write scopes for them. Slack approval depends on a model-set `external` flag (`app/gate.py:40`). Approvals bind the tool and target, never the arguments. |\n\n- **Prescan:** only H001 (`app/gate.py:35`) applied to this batch. I confirmed it under B05 and left the other hits for their own batches.\n- **Injection attempt:** one is recorded in `injection_attempts`. A fixture file (`t